 - 2026-08-29: Tool-gap feedback for the induction tool loop (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6770, worktree agent) — dispatch now retains the identity of refused tool calls (`tool_gap_events`: unknown_tool + bad_arguments), the loop and the live E3 repair record carry them, and a curated candidate-tool registry (`register_candidate_tool` + `CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_CANDIDATE_TOOLS`, default off, byte-identical unset) makes human-authored tool introduction measurable. Offline analyzer `scripts/arc_tool_gap_refine.py` builds `ops/arc_tool_gap_ledger.json` and writes human-only specifications; gap ledger `ops/arc_tool_gaps.md` seeded with the measured bootstrap state (633 live calls, zero unknown-name demand, 8 unidentifiable pre-capture failures). 17 tests at the induce() entry point, 15 mutations all RED. Design: docs/research-notes/arc-tool-gap-feedback-2026-08-29.md
 - 2026-08-29: artifact_freshness_lint worktree fix (same session) — run from a session worktree, `_repo_relative` could not strip another checkout's absolute prefix, so `drift_is_pre_existing` fail-closed and refused worktree commits for backlog they did not cause (observed live: three artifacts, every drifted dependency already drifted at HEAD, classified caused-here). Fallback now relativizes via the git toplevel containing the recorded path with GIT_* env stripped (git-commit hooks export GIT_DIR, which hijacked rev-parse into reporting the probe dir as toplevel); /tmp scratch paths still drop; unresolvable paths still fail closed. Regression test in tests/python/test_artifact_freshness_pre_existing_backlog_20260811.py, proven by deletion (RED). Two PRE-EXISTING failures noted, not fixed here: test_the_live_repo_artifact_is_registered_and_fresh (arc_gateway_card artifact stale at HEAD) and test_the_three_real_acknowledgements_are_complete_and_current (27 vs 2 acknowledgements in a 20260727 artifact).
 - 2026-08-29 (later, same worktree session): tool-gap feedback reworked after hostile review + coordinator directive — the unmerged first cut (a613f36bc7) was split: the artifact_freshness_lint fix is now its own commit (relatedness-gated worktree fallback, R1; GIT_DIR strip on the block-deciding head hash, R2; narrowed env denylist, R3), and the feature commit fixes the review's premise finding F2 (the primary live induction never recorded gap evidence — loop transports "1"/"selfparse" vs the widened record's "repair" branch are mutually exclusive values of one env var; the primary site now records attempt["tool_gap"]), plus F3/F4 name-first capture on refused calls, F5/F7 per-session enablement freeze, F6 dark-candidate coercion gate, F8 three decorative assertions replaced with biting tests (corrigendum: the earlier "zero decorative rules" claim was false), F9 event-string caps, F10 the bootstrap null rescoped to the server-lifted corpus. 30 mutation runs, all RED. Not merged to main per coordinator hold.
+- 2026-08-29: Lossless GGUF output boundary and 216-row reparse (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: lossless transport replay recovered 216/216 rows; 11/216 exact-valid is a separate semantic outcome; results/experiment_6755_lossless_gguf_output_reparse.json
